    "reasoning": "All 16 mathematical answers agree with their own captured MA solutions. Two authored notation errors remain: q-152124 drops the numerator 6 in its final displayed integral; that displayed integral would equal \\pi/12, whereas the actual question correctly equals \\pi/2. q-20502 writes dx instead of du in one transformed integral, but its substitution and final answer are correct. Calculations: q-85712 is the geometric series with ratio -x^2. q-152090 equals 8(-\\pi/4+\\pi/2)=2\\pi. q-152083 equals 4(\\pi/2+\\pi/3)=10\\pi/3. q-152124 equals 3(-\\pi/3+\\pi/2)=\\pi/2. q-6037 equals (2/3)(\\pi/2)=\\pi/3. q-119199 equals (1/\\sqrt{3})(\\pi/6+\\pi/2)=2\\pi/(3\\sqrt{3}). q-20502 becomes the integral of 1/(1+3u^2) from 1 to infinity, giving \\pi/(6\\sqrt{3})=\\sqrt{3}\\pi/18. q-162343 has p congruent to 4 modulo 6, and 4 is the valid offered representative. q-216349 equals -3(b cross a)=3i-6j+3k. Using downward-positive displacement s=ut+4.9t^2 gives q-10586: 44.1 m; q-135099: 5(5)+4.9(25)=147.5 m; q-135105: (600-176.4)/6=70.6 m/s; q-135223: (720-705.6)/12=1.2 m/s; q-10510: t=3 s; q-135228: (t+10)(t-5)=0, hence t=5 s. q-120657 uses tan^2(theta)=sec^2(theta)-1 and cancellation to obtain sec(theta)-1 on the original expression's domain. No submitted grade was provided; each MA answer is supported by its captured worked solution.",
